-- title:
--   Powers on the Igusa branch at a crossing node
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, and write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$; assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, Henselian local, with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Give $\overline{F} =$ `fieldBar q M'` (the full-level modular function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained from $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \overline{F}$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{F}$ and valuation subring $W_0 \subseteq F_0$ whose elements of $k_0$ are exactly those in $A$, which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; for every local Noetherian subring $O \subseteq F_0$ with $O \subseteq W_0$, whose elements of $k_0$ are exactly those in $A$, such that every $f \in O$ differs from the image of some $x \in k_0 \cap A$ by a non-unit of $O$, and such that every $f \in F_0$ satisfies $fh = g$ for some $g, h \in O$ with $h \ne 0$; for every $E_0 \ge 1$, with $\pi_0$ mapping into $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that ring, subject to $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$, to $\iota$ carrying the image of each $x \in k_0 \cap A$ to the corresponding constant `UVCrossingModel.const`, and to $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$, $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$; and for every valuation subring $W_x \subseteq F_0$ containing $O$ which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$, with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ outside it: every $b \in O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ satisfies $b^{E_0+1} = c_x m$ for some non-unit $m \in O$.
--
--   This is the local algebra of a node of the modular curve presented by a crossing model $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$: along the branch $W_x$ cut out by $c_x$, vanishing of $b$ to first order forces $c_x \mid b^{E_0+1}$ with non-unit cofactor. It is used in the construction of functions separating two nodes on a common chart and in the assembly of the node charts and Hasse/Igusa data at full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_pow_eq_mul_nonunit_of_mem_maximalIdeal_igusaBranch_of_node_crossingPresentation.lean

